 CHANGELOG.md | 5 +++++
 README.md    | 2 +-
 emil.1       | 9 ++++++++-
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 5765a20..c181638 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -17,6 +17,11 @@
 - Fixed `C-q` inserting an invalid byte, after which the buffer could not be
   saved, when a terminal resize interrupted it.
 - The advisory lock's file descriptor is no longer inherited by shell commands.
+- A file path must now be valid UTF-8 with no C0 control character or DEL.
+  Other paths are refused on opening and saving, a `cd` that would give an open
+  buffer such a name is refused, and one named on the command line makes `emil`
+  exit with an error. Rename such a file to edit it.
+- Fixed invalid UTF-8 from a tags file reaching the `M-.` definitions menu.
 
 ## [1.0.0] - 2026-10-12
 - `emil --help` added.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index f1e4138..7ae0ddd 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -169,7 +169,7 @@ Selections larger than  74,993 bytes are not sent to the clipboard and a status
 
 ## Internals
 
-Each buffer is an array of logical lines (`erow`) holding raw UTF-8 bytes. Every buffer contains only valid UTF-8; files that fail validation are rejected at load time. Rendering and text layout never modify the buffer.
+Each buffer is an array of logical lines (`erow`) holding raw UTF-8 bytes. Every buffer contains only valid UTF-8; files that fail validation are rejected at load time. A file path must be valid UTF-8 with no C0 control character or DEL: `emil` refuses other paths when opening or saving, refuses a `cd` that would give an open buffer such a name, and exits at startup if one is named on the command line. Rendering and text layout never modify the buffer.
 
 A row's display width is cached on the row and recomputed when the row is edited. The renderer calculates wrap positions only for the rows on screen, not for the whole buffer.
 
diff --git a/emil.1 b/emil.1
index 3335fa8..fd89f5a 100644
--- a/emil.1
+++ b/emil.1
@@ -496,6 +496,13 @@ Files are loaded in their entirety into memory.
 adheres to the Unix convention where lines are delimited by a single linefeed (LF) character and files terminate with a linefeed.
 A file opened without a terminating linefeed gains one when it is loaded.
 Validation at file load and inserting text in the buffer disallow  null bytes (0x00) or malformed UTF-8 sequences.
+.Pp
+A file path must be valid UTF-8 with no C0 control character or DEL.
+.Nm
+refuses any other path when opening a file, saving under a new name, or changing to a directory that would give an open buffer such a name.
+A file named on the command line with such a path makes
+.Nm
+exit at startup with an error; rename the file to edit it.
 .Ss File Persistence
 When saving,
 .Nm
@@ -515,7 +522,7 @@ begins to edit the file, it receives a warning. The lock does not prevent other
 is not designed for editing very large files. Files larger than 1 GiB cannot be opened.
 .Sh EXIT STATUS
 .Nm
-exits 0 on success and 1 if a file cannot be opened, an unrecognised
+exits 0 on success and 1 if a file cannot be opened or its path is refused, an unrecognised
 option is given, or standard output is not a terminal.
 .Sh SEE ALSO
 .Xr emacs 1
